            <ArticleTitle>[Pulmological aspects of diagnosis of thoracic pain (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>747-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A number of medical disciplines are involved in the diagnosis and therapy of thoracic pain. The origin may be somatic or visceral. Individual diseases are discussed in particular such as myalgia epidemica, intercostal neuralgia, herpes zoster, pleuritis and pneumonia, pulmonary embolism, pneumothorax, mediastinal emphysema, mediastinitis, pulmonary hypertension and the hyperventilation syndrome. Differential diagnosis is also referred to.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
